Implement Stack using Array

Implement a stack with fixed capacity n. Support:
1. push(x) - Insert x at top (ignore if full)
2. pop() - Remove top (ignore if empty)
3. peek() - Return top or -1 if empty
4. isEmpty() - Return true if empty
5. isFull() - Return true if full

Input: n (capacity), q (queries), queries[][]
- [1, x] → push(x)
- [2] → pop()
- [3] → peek()
- [4] → isEmpty()
- [5] → isFull()

Constraints:
- 1 ≤ n, q ≤ 10³
- 0 ≤ x ≤ 10⁵


Your Approach: ArrayList-based stack
- Use ArrayList's end as stack top
- Delegate operations to ArrayList methods
- Check isFull() before push, isEmpty() before pop/peek

Time: O(1) per operation | Space: O(n)
